1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,440
Hello, and welcome to a CAD Guilds tutorial on data science.

2
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:13,400
In this video, we will explain the difference between three key concepts, artificial intelligence,

3
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:19,120
machine learning, and deep learning, to understand how they relate to the field of data science.

4
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,179
First up, artificial intelligence, or AI.

5
00:00:22,179 --> 00:00:24,179
What is it?

6
00:00:24,179 --> 00:00:29,480
Artificial intelligence is simply any code, technique, or algorithm that enables machines

7
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:34,359
to mimic, develop, and demonstrate human cognition or behavior.

8
00:00:34,359 --> 00:00:38,600
We are in what many refer to as the era of weak AI.

9
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:43,840
The technology is still in its infancy and is expected to make machines capable of doing

10
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:48,799
anything and everything humans do in the era of strong AI.

11
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:54,540
To transition from weak AI to strong AI, machines need to learn the ways of humans.

12
00:00:54,539 --> 00:01:00,700
The techniques and processes which help machines in this endeavor are broadly categorized under

13
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:02,619
machine learning.

14
00:01:02,619 --> 00:01:04,980
Machines learn in predominantly two ways.

15
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:08,939
Their learning is either supervised or unsupervised.

16
00:01:08,939 --> 00:01:14,819
In supervised learning, machines learn to predict outcomes with help from data scientists.

17
00:01:14,819 --> 00:01:20,099
In unsupervised learning, machines learn to predict outcomes on the go by recognizing

18
00:01:20,099 --> 00:01:22,579
patterns in input data.

19
00:01:22,579 --> 00:01:28,140
When machines can draw meaningful inferences from large volumes of data sets, they demonstrate

20
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,579
the ability to learn deeply.

21
00:01:30,579 --> 00:01:36,620
Deep learning requires artificial neural networks, ANNs, which are like the biological neural

22
00:01:36,620 --> 00:01:38,700
networks in humans.

23
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:43,099
These networks contain nodes in different layers that are connected and communicate with

24
00:01:43,099 --> 00:01:46,980
each other to make sense of voluminous input data.

25
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:52,820
Deep learning is a subset of machine learning, which in turn is a subset of artificial intelligence.

26
00:01:52,820 --> 00:01:58,659
The three technologies help scientists and analysts interpret tons of data and are hence

27
00:01:58,659 --> 00:02:01,500
crucial for the field of data science.

28
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:06,700
To learn more about these technologies, subscribe to AcadGild's blog and YouTube channel.

